==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.07~6 seconds<sup>2f~180f</sup>.
*2 [[Shibalien Elite]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[THE SLOTH]] spawns as the boss.
**15 [[Shibalien Elite]]s spawn, delay 13.33~26.67 seconds<sup>400f~800f</sup>.
**3 [[St. Pigge the 2nd]]s spawn, delay 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
**3 [[St. Pigge the 2nd]]s spawn, delay 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
**3 [[Corporal Weyland]]s spawn, delay 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Make sure you have all [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]] by this point, and this stage will become a joke even with their magnifications: the Corporal Weylands are not that much of a threat, THE SLOTH attacks too infrequently, and the St. Pigge the 2nds are the only frontliners. Use [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]], [[Bath Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Luxury Bath Cat]], [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], and other [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]] cats to rush down the St. Pigge the 2nds. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] along with [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] and [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] should be everything else you need to win.

